  :adr/decision-summary
  "New repo kotoba-lang/pricing-oracle: pure .cljc core (predict-band) that predicts a price band for gap verticals (no real self-serve price found) from other verticals that ARE priced, via a 4-stage fallback most-specific-first: same-cluster+same-unit -> same-cluster any-unit (dominant path) -> same-unit any-cluster -> shape-family (cross-industry, always low confidence). Every prediction carries basis-vertical-ids. Predictions are namespaced :pred/* and written to the oracle's own predictions.edn, never back into cloud-itonami's pricing-intelligence-ledger.edn, to keep real-research vs model-estimate provenance separate. Verified: 29 nbb tests pass; real run against 211-vertical cloud-itonami dataset resolved all 74 gaps at :medium confidence via cluster-fallback."
  :adr/result
  "29/29 nbb unit tests pass (test/pricing_oracle/core_test.cljs). Real run: 211 verticals loaded, 137 with real bands, 74 gaps, all 74 predicted via :cluster-fallback at :confidence :medium, checked in as orgs/kotoba-lang/pricing-oracle/predictions.edn."
  :adr/github-url "https://github.com/kotoba-lang/pricing-oracle"}]
